-- The 74 spells Rifts World Book 7: Underseas defines, across four separate
-- magic traditions.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-underseas-spells.sql
--
-- The book is a SCAN with no text layer. Offsets come from scripts/books.json:
-- page_offset -1 with an exception putting printed 1-130 at +0. The Ocean,
-- Spellsong and Dolphin chapters all sit BELOW the split, so printed N is
-- cache pN; the two Korallyte spells sit above it, so printed 151 is cache
-- p150 and printed 152 is p151.
--
--   tradition               printed    rows   stored as
--   Whale Singer Spellsongs   57-60      21    Spellsong:
--   Ocean Magic               63-70      41    Ocean:
--   Dolphin Magic             70-72      10    Dolphin:
--   Korallyte Shaping        151-152      2    unprefixed
--
-- EVERY COST HAS TWO INDEPENDENT READINGS for 72 of the 74. Each of the first
-- three chapters opens with its own alphabetical list printing Name (cost),
-- and each description then repeats the figure on its own P.P.E.: line. All 72
-- agree. The two Korallyte spells have no list and are transcribed once.
--
-- LEVELS DO NOT HAVE A SECOND READING, and the three traditions state them
-- three different ways:
--
--   Ocean Magic     a Level: line in every stat block. 41 of 41 present.
--   Dolphin Magic   a Level: line in every stat block. 10 of 10 present.
--   Korallyte       IN THE HEADING - "Shape Koral (Level Four)" - and the stat
--                   block carries no Level: line at all.
--   Spellsongs      NOWHERE. See the level 0 note below.
--
-- TWO OCR READINGS WERE CONFIRMED AGAINST RENDERED PAGES rather than inferred.
-- The ocean chapter's Level: lines render "5th" as "Sth" and "1st" as "Ist"
-- throughout - no correctly-spelled 5th or 1st appears anywhere in the chapter,
-- while 3rd, 6th, 7th and 8th all read cleanly, so the two digits are
-- systematically mangled in that one position. Printed 65 and 66 were rendered
-- at 200 dpi and read directly: "Communicate with Sea Creature ... Level: 5th"
-- and "Metamorphosis Crustacean ... Level: 11th" (OCR "1 1th"). Both hold.
--
-- SPELLSONGS ARE LEVEL 0, deliberately, on the add-wormwood-prayers.sql
-- precedent. The book gives them no level at all: printed 57 has the Whale
-- Singer select four at level one, two at level two and one per level after
-- that, so there is nothing for a level column to hold. A class granting them
-- names them through magic.spells_from, and leveling.js states that a named
-- list REPLACES the spell-level gate - so 0 gates nothing rather than gating
-- them out.
--
-- THE PREFIXES ARE FORCED, NOT DECORATIVE, and this is the important part of
-- this file. TEN of these 74 share a name with a row the catalog already
-- holds, and in every case the two are THE SAME SPELL published for a
-- different tradition at a different level and a different price:
--
--   this book (ocean)                catalog (Water Warlock, Book of Magic)
--   Change Current               15   Water: Change Current              L2/8
--   Communicate with Sea Creature10   Water: Communicate with Sea Cr.   L4/12
--   Float on Water                3   Water: Float on Water             L1/4
--   Impervious to Ocean Depths   75   Water: Impervious to Ocean Depths L3/12
--   Ride the Waves               10   Water: Ride the Waves             L2/7
--   Sense Direction Underwater    4   Water: Sense Direction Underwater L1/4
--   Speak Underwater             10   Water: Speak Underwater           L4/10
--   Water Seal                   10   Water: Water Seal                 L2/8
--   Whirlpool                L9/ 50   Water: Whirlpool                  L5/40
--   Sonic Blast (dolphin)    L5/ 15   Sonic Blast                       L7/25
--
-- THAT THEY ARE THE SAME SPELL WAS CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED. Water: Whirlpool was
-- read out of production and compared against printed 70 line by line: same
-- 120 foot radius, same 500 foot casting range, same ten feet per melee round
-- drag, same 20 foot centre, same drowning percentages. The Book of Magic
-- publishes it at level 5 for 40 P.P.E.; Underseas publishes it at level 9 for
-- 50. Neither is wrong and neither supersedes the other - they are two
-- traditions pricing one effect.
--
-- One row cannot hold both, because the sheet's use button spends spells.ppe.
-- So the ocean list takes an Ocean: prefix and the dolphin list a Dolphin:
-- one, following the Water: / Fire: / Air: / Earth: families the catalog
-- already uses for a scoped tradition - 231 rows of precedent. Each colliding
-- row carries the warlock reading in variant_note, so the disagreement is on
-- the record rather than lost. The modelling gap is BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26.
--
-- The two Korallyte spells are stored UNPREFIXED. Shape Koral and Koral Blast
-- collide with nothing, the names are unique and self-identifying, and a
-- two-row family does not need a prefix to be legible in a picker.
--
-- NOT IMPORTED, and this is a deliberate omission rather than a gap: printed
-- 63 carries a second list headed "Additional Spell Magic for Ocean Wizards",
-- 36 spells the book names FROM THE CORE RIFTS RPG by page number so that an
-- Ocean Wizard may learn them. Every one is already in this catalog. It is a
-- grant list belonging in the Ocean Wizard's magic block, not new data.
--
-- ONE THING THE BOOK DOES NOT EXPLAIN. Its ocean list marks Calm Waters with
-- an asterisk and prints no footnote anywhere on the page - checked in both
-- the clean and the raw OCR. The description's only cross-reference is to
-- Calm Storms, which is one of the 36 core spells listed just below it, so the
-- asterisk MAY mark "see the related core spell". That is an inference and it
-- is not stored anywhere as fact.
--
-- ON CONFLICT (name) DO UPDATE rather than INSERT OR IGNORE, so this file is
-- the authoritative bytes in every environment even where a row already
-- exists. Pure ASCII with LF endings on purpose - see PR #101.

INSERT INTO spells
  (name, level, ppe, ppe_note, variant_note, source, source_book, system, range, duration, damage, saving_throw, area_of_effect, casting_time, description)
VALUES
  ('Spellsong: Song of Calling', 0, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.57', 'rifts', '300 miles (482 km) per level of experience.', 'Five minutes.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'Lets the singer hold a two-way conversation with one named person at great distance, but only if that person accepts the call; otherwise the song fails automatically. A single casting carries five minutes of conversation.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Danger', 0, 4, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; ten times that for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'A warning song telling other whale singers and cetaceans whether a danger is immediate, minor or terrible and which way it is heading. A whale singer can also tell what the danger is - hunters, D-bees, monsters, minions of the Lord of the Deep, Reachers.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Doubt', 0, 6, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'Everyone who hears it becomes nervous and unconfident, and is likely to hang back or take a different route away from the song. Those affected are -2 on initiative and -20% on all skill performance.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Fear', 0, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'A deep moaning that unsettles even those who save. A character who fails begs his companions to retreat; if attacked by whale singers, pneuma-biforms, killer whales or frightening non-humans he is petrified - no initiative, and attacks, combat bonuses and skill performance all halved - his attackers carry a horror factor of 15, and there is a 50% chance he panics and flees. A second successful save leaves him with half those penalties.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Grief', 0, 2, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'A mourning song that everyone who hears it, even a surface dweller, understands as telling of death or tragedy. Compassionate characters, and even selfish or evil ones, leave the singers alone; a truly heartless villain may instead use the distraction to strike.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Joy', 0, 4, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'A celebratory song that can only be sung in safety and happiness, never to lure an enemy or where danger, death or sorrow is present. It repels sharks, entities, ghouls, animated dead and lesser demons, and leaves minions of the Lord of the Deep -1 on initiative and on all combat moves.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Life', 0, 750, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', 'Ten feet (3.0 m)', 'The ritual takes twenty minutes to one hour; the restoration is instant.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'A ritual variant of the whales'' mourning chants that heals all damage and removes any curse, crippling injury or disease from one person, human, D-bee or cetacean. It can raise the recently dead: a base 40% chance plus 5% per level of the caster, less 5% for every day since the death.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Protection', 0, 35, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', 'Self', 'As long as the song is sung, and up to fifteen minutes per level of the singer after it stops.', NULL, 'None', NULL, 'One melee round.', 'Grants an aura of protection worth 60 M.D.C. against every form of damage, and makes the recipient invulnerable to deep sea pressure, extreme cold and heat, and any environmental hazard short of a star''s corona.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Revenge', 0, 400, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.58', 'rifts', 'Unlimited', 'Permanent', '3D6 direct to hit points, or 6D6 if the victim is a mega-damage creature.', '18 or higher on an unmodified, natural roll.', NULL, '1D6 hours.', 'A curse sung against someone known beyond doubt to have committed a grave crime against the pneuma-biforms, whales, dolphins or the sea. A victim who fails takes the damage above, is marked with a visible purple whale-shaped blemish, and is -1 on all combat rolls and -5% on all skills until the curse is lifted, usually by an act of atonement. None of it can be healed by any scientific, magical or psionic means. The Lord of the Deep is impervious to it.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Reversal', 0, 500, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', 'Ten feet (3.0 m)', 'Permanent', NULL, 'Special; the target resists at +3 to save.', NULL, NULL, 'A ritual needing at least four singers that un-fuses one of the Lord of the Deep''s composite minions back into the creatures it was made from. Success separates them for a duration scaling with the lead singer''s level, with a 1-67% chance of being permanent, and the same song safely detaches a magic symbiote from its host. It does not work on a true pneuma-biform, a victim of a transformation ritual, a god-altered being or a natural shapeshifter.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Severing', 0, 110, NULL, 'The book labels this entry''s casting time "Casting Time:" where the other two entries carrying one - Song of Protection and Song of Revenge - label it "Casting Time Required:". The book disagreeing with itself, not a reading.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', 'One mile (1.6 km) per level of experience.', 'Instant', '2D6x1000 M.D. to the Lord of the Deep itself.', 'Standard', NULL, '1D6+2 melee rounds.', 'An anti-Reacher ritual cast within sight of a Reacher tentacle while allies defend the singer. Success destroys the tentacle, tripling the time it takes to regrow, and inflicts the damage above on the Lord of the Deep.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Sea Sickness', 0, 50, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung, and 2D6 minutes after.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'A victim who fails is nauseous and headachey: -10% on skill performance, speed cut by 30%, no initiative, and a strong urge to vomit under any exertion.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Sleep', 0, 30, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung, and 2D6 minutes after.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'Even a character who saves becomes drowsy: -2 on initiative, -10% and slower on skills, and less alert. One who fails falls asleep within 1D4 minutes and wakes only to rough shaking, and if forced awake fights at half effectiveness, 75% reduced speed and no initiative.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Strength', 0, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', 'Self, plus chosen others within 1000 feet (305 m).', 'Five minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Grants the singer and one recipient per level +10 to P.S., ten times normal carrying and lifting capacity, and immunity to fatigue. A variant of the same song repels undead and haunting entities within 1000 feet.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Summoning', 0, 200, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', '50 miles (80 km) per level of experience.', 'Instant', NULL, 'Special; an unwilling target saves as standard, at +6 if the two are enemies.', NULL, NULL, 'A stronger form of the Song of Calling that teleports a known, willing person instantly to the caster. A target who resists successfully cannot be summoned again for a week.'),
  ('Spellsong: Song of Weaving', 0, 150, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', 'Touch', 'Permanent', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Weaves kelp into body armor that shapes itself to a humanoid or a cetacean and provides 90 M.D.C. Once that is gone the armor falls apart and must be woven again.'),
  ('Spellsong: Sonic Boom', 0, 40, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.59', 'rifts', '200 feet (61 m) plus 100 feet (30.5 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant', '1D4x10 M.D. plus 10 M.D. per level to the primary target and 4D6 M.D. to everything else within a 100 foot radius. In air the range halves and the damage drops to 5D6 M.D. to the main target and 1D4 M.D. within ten feet.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'A directed underwater blast strong enough to endanger the singer''s own allies. Even mega-damage creatures and armoured or bionic characters caught in the radius are left ringing and dizzy - -1 to strike, parry and dodge, -20% to swim, climb, run or navigate, and -10% speed - for 1D6 melee rounds underwater or 1D4 in air, and repeated blasts add their durations together.'),
  ('Spellsong: Sound Blast', 0, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.60', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant', 'A light blast does 1D6x10 S.D.C. and can be fired twice per casting; a mega-damage blast does 1D6 M.D. per level of the caster but only once per casting.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'An ultrasonic strike the book likens to a torpedo hit, cast at either of two power tiers.'),
  ('Spellsong: Sound Spike', 0, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.60', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant against a living target; two minutes per level against electronics.', '2D6, S.D.C. or M.D. depending on the victim.', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'A painful sonic spike that also costs the victim two melee actions and his initiative. A successful save, sound filtration, ear protection, or being inside armor or a vehicle halves both the damage and the lost actions. A humming variant instead jams radio, sonar and sound-based sensors for the duration and does no damage.'),
  ('Spellsong: Stormsong', 0, 250, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.60', 'rifts', 'One square mile (2.59 sq km) per level of experience.', 'Thirty minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Turns calm ocean to storm or storm to calm, with twenty foot waves and driving rain at its worst. It can capsize a small craft, cuts a larger ship''s speed by 75%, and sickens 2D4x10% of a crew. It has no effect on anyone more than a hundred feet below the surface.'),
  ('Spellsong: Valorsong', 0, 50, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.60', 'rifts', '1000 feet (305 m) distance and radius per level of experience; double for a humpback whale.', 'As long as the song is sung, and 2D6 minutes after.', NULL, 'Standard', NULL, NULL, 'Heartens the singer''s allies: +4 to save versus horror factor, +2 versus poison and disease, and +1 versus illusion and mind control.'),
  ('Ocean: Abilities of a Snail', 7, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'Self or another person by touch.', 'Two minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Grows magical antennae and gives the recipient a snail''s adhesion, letting him climb any surface including a vessel moving up to 100 mph, at 60-80% of normal running and climbing speed. The antennae sense water temperature, current, and blood or chemicals at half a mile, and motion within 20 feet, giving +1 to dodge and cutting blindness penalties by 75%. The recipient can carry twice his body weight, survives to 1000 feet, and is +10% to prowl.'),
  ('Ocean: Air Swim', 6, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'Self or one other by touch.', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'The recipient swims through air with the same speed and agility he has underwater, up to ten feet above the surface per level of the caster. Useful for escaping foes that cannot fly. A character who must stay wet can dip back into the water periodically; he dries out after about twenty minutes.'),
  ('Ocean: Armor of Neptune', 6, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'Self or another by touch.', 'Three minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Grants breathable air, immunity to cold with half damage from magical cold, immunity to depth and pressure, and an invisible force armor worth 15 M.D.C. per level of the caster.'),
  ('Ocean: Black Water', 2, 5, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'Up to 100 feet (30.5 m) away, +10 feet (3 m) per level of experience.', 'One minute per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard; fish and animals need an 18 or higher.', NULL, NULL, 'Turns an area of water inky black. Predators and intelligent creatures avoid it. Anyone entering is blinded and disoriented, loses initiative, and has attacks, bonuses and skill performance halved by panic; the disorientation persists 1D4 melee rounds after leaving.'),
  ('Ocean: Breathe Air', 3, 5, NULL, 'The book heads this entry Breathe Air (without gills) and lists it as Breathe Air on printed 63.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'Self or two others.', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Lets a gilled creature breathe air the way a mammal does, so an aquatic character can operate on dry land.'),
  ('Ocean: Calm Waters', 11, 150, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'One mile (1.6 km) radius per level of experience.', 'One hour per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Stills a body of water without freezing it. Waves calm, though waterfalls still fall. It suppresses waterspouts, tsunamis, underwater explosions and quakes, and pacifies an angry water elemental, which will still defend itself. The effect centres on the caster but persists after he leaves, and stops at the edge of the radius.'),
  ('Ocean: Change Current', 6, 15, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Change Current" at level 2 for 8 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.83. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 6 for 15. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.64', 'rifts', 'The current nearest the caster; affects a 1000 foot (305 m) radius per level of experience.', 'Five minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Reverses or redirects an isolated ocean current. Used to move an adrift ship or wreckage, disperse pollution, or confuse fish and sailors.'),
  ('Ocean: Communicate with Sea Creature', 5, 10, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Communicate with Sea Creature" at level 4 for 12 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.85. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 5 for 10. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m)', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Telepathic dialogue with any sea creature, including fish, sea mammals and many aquatic predators from other worlds, but not underwater plants, invertebrates or intelligent beings. A dialogue does not mean the creature will obey, cooperate, or tell the truth.'),
  ('Ocean: Coral Armor', 7, 10, 'Ten for S.D.C. armor, or 45 for M.D.C. armor.', NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self', 'Five minutes per level of the spell caster.', '2D4 S.D.C. to anyone who touches the armor.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Forms lightweight, noiseless living coral armor worth 15 S.D.C. or 15 M.D.C. per level of the caster, the choice deciding the cost. Lightning, cold and water attacks do one third damage. The armor is neither air-tight nor water-tight.'),
  ('Ocean: Float Underwater', 2, 5, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or two others.', 'Fifteen minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'The recipient becomes buoyant enough to float underwater without sinking below 1000 feet or rising to the surface. A swimmer can still direct himself, at half the usual exhaustion.'),
  ('Ocean: Float on Water', 1, 3, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Float on Water" at level 1 for 4 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.82. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 1 for 3. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or two others; can be cast up to 30 feet (9 m) away.', 'Thirty minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Makes the target buoyant enough to float on the surface like driftwood. It does not grant the ability to swim, but a swimmer can steer and swim against the current at half the usual exhaustion.'),
  ('Ocean: Flying Fish', 3, 8, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or two others by touch.', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'The recipient leaps from the water and glides up to twenty feet above the waves at roughly 40 mph, covering 100 feet per level of the caster in a single glide before diving back in. He can repeat the leap until the duration ends.'),
  ('Ocean: Grow Tentacles', 8, 30, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or one person by touch.', 'Two minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Grows a pair of tentacles per casting, cumulative to three pairs, each tentacle having 60 M.D.C. Every pair adds one melee attack, +1 to strike and parry, and +1 on initiative.'),
  ('Ocean: Healing Waters', 6, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Three feet (0.9 m) per level of experience.', 'Two minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Turns a radius of water three feet per level into warm healing water that restores 1D6 S.D.C. or M.D.C. for every minute of exposure. It reverts to ordinary water when the spell ends.'),
  ('Ocean: Impervious to Cold', 4, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or one other by touch.', 'Twenty minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Grants complete immunity to cold, including the freezing temperatures of the deep ocean.'),
  ('Ocean: Impervious to Electricity', 7, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or one other by touch.', 'Fifteen minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Grants immunity to electricity, which does no damage. Magical lightning and electricity do half damage instead.'),
  ('Ocean: Impervious to Ocean Depths', 10, 75, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Impervious to Ocean Depths" at level 3 for 12 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.84. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 10 for 75. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.65', 'rifts', 'Self or two others by touch.', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Immunity to deep ocean pressure, allowing travel to the deepest trenches. If the spell lapses at depth the character is crushed instantly; for an unarmoured human any depth past 250 feet is lethal.'),
  ('Ocean: Metamorphosis Crustacean', 11, 60, 'Sixty, or 120 for a monster crustacean.', NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.66', 'rifts', 'Self or one person; can be cast up to 30 feet (9 m) away.', 'Ten minutes per level of the spell caster.', 'Normal form: 1 S.D.C. pincer for a tiny or small crustacean, 1D4 S.D.C. for a large one, two attacks per melee. Monster form: 3D6 M.D. pincer or claw, 1D6 M.D. body block or stomp, four attacks per melee.', 'Standard, if the recipient tries to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Transforms the caster into a crab, lobster or shrimp no smaller than half an inch and no longer than three feet, or into a giant monster crustacean at the higher cost. He keeps his I.Q. and memory but cannot use skills, speak, or cast magic while transformed.'),
  ('Ocean: Metamorphosis Fish', 9, 50, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.67', 'rifts', 'Self or one person; can be cast up to 30 feet (9 m) away.', 'Ten minutes per level of the spell caster.', 'Bite 1D4 S.D.C. for a medium fish or 2D4 S.D.C. for a large one, 2D6 for a barracuda. Tail slap 1D6 S.D.C. medium, 2D6 large, swordfish or marlin.', 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Transforms the caster into a large or medium fish, but not a jellyfish, starfish or sea mammal. He keeps his mental attributes but cannot use skills, speak or cast while transformed. Grants gill breathing, a 15 mph swim with bursts to 40 mph, +1 on initiative, +2 to dodge, and survival to two miles depth.'),
  ('Ocean: Metamorphosis Shark', 12, 90, 'Ninety, or 160 for a monster shark.', NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.67', 'rifts', 'Self or one person; can be cast up to 30 feet (9 m) away.', 'Ten minutes per level of the spell caster.', 'Bite 4D6 S.D.C.; power bite or rip 1D6x10 S.D.C., counting as two melee attacks; tail slap 2D6 S.D.C., mega-damage as a monster shark.', 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Transforms the caster into a large shark, or a monster shark at the higher cost. He keeps his mental attributes but loses skills, speech and spell casting. Grants an electrical sense, blood scent tracking to two miles at 80%, nightvision to 500 feet, combat bonuses, +3D6x10 bonus S.D.C. or M.D.C., and survival to three miles depth.'),
  ('Ocean: Mystic Sea Horse', 6, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.67', 'rifts', 'Immediate area; speed up to 40 mph (64 km).', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Conjures a giant water elemental sea horse that a humanoid can ride or others can cling to. It is of low intelligence and can travel to four miles depth.'),
  ('Ocean: Ride the Waves', 5, 10, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Ride the Waves" at level 2 for 7 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.83. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 5 for 10. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.67', 'rifts', 'Self and/or two others; speed up to 40 mph (64 km).', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Creates a magical wave the caster can ride without a board, and which others can ride although only the caster steers. It can also tow a small boat at half speed.'),
  ('Ocean: Sense Direction Underwater', 1, 4, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Sense Direction Underwater" at level 1 for 4 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.82. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 1 for 4. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.67', 'rifts', 'Self', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Grants a flawless sense of direction, of changes in the direction and speed of the current, and accurate depth perception, even in complete darkness.'),
  ('Ocean: Senses of the Shark', 6, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.67', 'rifts', 'Self', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Grants a shark''s blood scent tracking to two miles at 80%, an electrical sense, nightvision to 500 feet, +1 to save versus horror factor and +1 on initiative, all underwater only. It costs -20% on skill performance and carries a 15-80% chance, rising with exposure to blood, of an uncontrollable fighting frenzy in which the character may strike allies before recognising them.'),
  ('Ocean: Sonar Hearing', 4, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Self or two others by touch; sonar range 300 feet (91 m) +100 feet (30.5 m) per level of experience.', 'Two minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Grants bat-like echo-location to see underwater while blinded or in murky water. It is less precise than a dolphin''s: a character relying on it while blind is -1 on initiative, -1 to strike, and -2 to parry and dodge.'),
  ('Ocean: Sound Sponge', 7, 30, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Can be cast up to 500 feet (152 m) away.', 'Five minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Creates a bubble twenty feet in diameter per level that absorbs all sound, including sonar and sonic probes, so that it appears as a void to detection. An expanded globe of silence.'),
  ('Ocean: Speak Underwater', 4, 10, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Speak Underwater" at level 4 for 10 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.85. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 4 for 10. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Self or two others by touch.', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, but only if the recipient resists.', NULL, NULL, 'Lets a surface dweller speak underwater as easily as in air, audible at 100 feet +10 feet per level of experience.'),
  ('Ocean: Strength of the Whale', 7, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Self', 'Five minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient desires to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Doubles P.S. and makes it supernatural, so punches do mega-damage. Doubles depth tolerance, roughly 500 feet extra for a human, doubles S.D.C. or adds 50% M.D.C. for a mega-damage being, halves the fatigue rate, and allows twenty foot leaps out of the water.'),
  ('Ocean: Summon Sea Friend', 8, 40, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'One mile (1.6 km) radius.', 'One hour per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Summons one friendly animal, rolled from dolphin, killer whale, sea otter, grey seal, manta ray or sea turtle; never a shark or a monster. It telepathically assists with any request that is not hostile, and the spell breaks if it leaves the one mile radius.'),
  ('Ocean: Transmute Water', 7, 15, 'Fifteen to change salt water to fresh or the reverse; 25 to also purify it completely.', NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Touch, or up to three feet (0.9 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Converts ten gallons of water per level between salt and fresh. An additional ten P.P.E., bringing the total to 25, also purifies toxins, pollutants and bacteria.'),
  ('Ocean: Travel Above Water', 8, 30, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Self and 100 lbs (45 kg).', 'One hour per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'The caster travels one to twelve inches above the waves at his normal ground speed and stays completely dry. A combined strength of 30 or more can drag him under, though the spell keeps trying to return him to the surface.'),
  ('Ocean: Walk Like a Humanoid', 8, 30, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.68', 'rifts', 'Self or one creature by touch.', 'Twenty minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'Standard, if the recipient tries to resist.', NULL, NULL, 'Gives an aquatic creature, or the caster, a pair of magical working legs to walk and run on land at a speed of 4D6. It does nothing about hydration or breathing air.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Envelope', 4, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', 'Self or two others by touch.', 'Ten minutes per level of experience.', 'The field has 20 M.D.C. before it collapses.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Encases an aquatic being that needs water in a force field envelope of circulating water, which also lets an air breather such as a dolphin breathe. It cannot be cast on a human or other surface dweller.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Nourishment', 5, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', 'Touch, or up to three feet (0.9 m) away.', 'Instant', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Converts eight fluid ounces of water into a nourishing nectar that sustains a person or a man-sized sea animal for a day.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Pulse', 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m)', 'Instant', '2D6 S.D.C., and a knockback of 1D4x10 yards/metres.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'A blast of water that knocks a human-sized target backward. Used to startle a foe, scatter fish, or disarm someone with a called shot.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Spout', 5, 12, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m), and 10 feet (3 m) above the waves.', 'Two minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Creates a column of water, used to signal, to lift the caster to a vantage point, or to capsize a boat: 50% for a small boat or raft, 30% for a medium vessel, 10% for a large one, and no chance against a carrier.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Rush', 5, 15, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m)', 'Instant', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'An underwater jet of current that sweeps victims thirty feet per level away. A victim needs a 15 or higher, rolled as a parry, to keep hold of his possessions, and takes 2D4 melee rounds to retrieve anything dropped. It can target one person or a swath twenty feet wide.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Seal', 5, 10, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Water Seal" at level 2 for 8 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.83. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 5 for 10. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', 'Touch, or up to three feet (0.9 m) away.', 'One hour per level of experience; triple for a sea druid.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Makes any container air-tight and water-resistant whatever it is made of, covering up to two cubic feet per level. It also seals a leaking door, hatch or porthole.'),
  ('Ocean: Water Wall', 7, 10, 'Ten for an S.D.C. wall, or 25 for an M.D.C. wall.', NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m) +10 feet (3 m) per level of experience.', 'One minute per level of experience.', '1D6x10 S.D.C. or 1D6x10 M.D. to whatever strikes it, and speed is cut by one third or one half.', 'None per se; dodge only.', NULL, NULL, 'Raises a standing wall of water five feet tall and ten feet long per level. It stops S.D.C. and M.D.C. projectiles and deflects lasers and large missiles at -5 to strike. It cannot be destroyed, reforming continuously from the ocean. Cast underwater it has half damage and half duration.'),
  ('Ocean: Weed Snare', 4, 8, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.69', 'rifts', 'Can be cast up to 100 feet (30.5 m) away.', 'Two melee rounds per level of experience.', NULL, 'Roll to save by pulling free.', NULL, NULL, 'Animates real seaweed to ensnare one target. Even a mega-damage being loses two melee actions struggling. An ensnared character can still fight and cast, but at -2 to strike, -4 to parry and -6 to dodge, and cannot move far. An S.D.C. creature can slip free on a successful save within 1D4 melee rounds.'),
  ('Ocean: Whirlpool', 9, 50, NULL, 'THE SAME SPELL is published as the Water Warlock invocation "Water: Whirlpool" at level 5 for 40 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.86. Underseas prints it as ocean magic at level 9 for 50. Two traditions, two prices, and one row cannot hold both - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.70', 'rifts', '120 foot (36.5 m) radius; can be cast up to 500 feet (153 m) away.', 'One minute per level of the spell caster.', '1D4x10 M.D. per melee round to a small object at the centre, 2D6x10 M.D. to a large ship, sub or bot. Being pulled under does 1D6x10 M.D. to a small item or person and 2D6x100 M.D. to a large vessel.', 'Not applicable.', NULL, NULL, 'Conjures a spinning whirlpool that drags everything on the water toward its centre at ten feet per melee round. A swimmer has a 50% chance of drowning in 2D4 minutes unless rescued. Most medium and large ships can pull out of the outer edge; a small vessel or life raft has a 50% chance. A dispel magic barrier destroys it instantly.'),
  ('Dolphin: Air Doubler', 4, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.70', 'rifts', 'Self or one other; can be cast on a person up to 100 feet (30.5 m) away.', 'Special', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'The recipient can hold his breath twice as long as usual. It works only on air already in living lungs and does nothing for an air tank.'),
  ('Dolphin: Electromagnetic Pulse', 5, 12, NULL, 'The book heads this entry Electro-Magnetic Pulse and lists it as Electromagnetic Pulse on printed 70. The list is the authority for membership, so the list spelling is stored and the heading is recorded here.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.70', 'rifts', 'Ten feet (3.0 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant', NULL, 'Special', NULL, NULL, 'Directs an electromagnetic pulse at electronics. A small underwater vehicle has a 1-60% chance of stalling or having its controls scrambled for 1D6 melee rounds, with its instruments out for 3D6 rounds. Worn armor or power armor loses targeting and scanners for 1D4 rounds and communications for 2D4. A submarine, large robot or ship sensor array is shielded and saves automatically.'),
  ('Dolphin: Psi-Flash Warning', 7, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.70', 'rifts', '1000 miles (1600 km) plus 300 miles (482.7 km) per level of experience.', 'Instant', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Sends an instantaneous and unmistakable telepathic warning to a known recipient or a general area, optionally carrying an image of the danger or the enemy''s face. The caster chooses whether to reveal his identity.'),
  ('Dolphin: Ride Ley Lines', 5, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.70', 'rifts', 'Self or one other; can be cast on a person up to 100 feet (30.5 m) away.', 'Special', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Quadruples swimming speed and breath-holding endurance while the recipient stays on a ley line; leaving the line ends it. It also grants awareness of ley line storms and Rift activity, and +2 on initiative and +2 to dodge while riding the line.'),
  ('Dolphin: Sense Food', 2, 6, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.71', 'rifts', 'Self or one other; can be cast on a person up to 100 feet (30.5 m) away.', 'Special', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Detects the rough distance and direction of nearby food - small fish, squid, shrimp, krill and invertebrates.'),
  ('Dolphin: Sense Predator', 3, 8, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.71', 'rifts', 'Self; the sensing area is a 200 foot (61 m) radius per level of experience.', 'Five minutes per level of experience.', NULL, 'None for animals. An intelligent creature rolls to save versus psionic probe, needing a 15 or higher.', NULL, NULL, 'Warns of nearby animal predators such as sharks, giant squid and mutant hunters, and gives a rough sense of their number and closeness. It also flags an intelligent hunter, who gets a save to stay hidden; one who resists is +6 to save against any further casting by anyone for ten minutes.'),
  ('Dolphin: Sense Weather', 4, 10, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.71', 'rifts', 'Self; weather within a 200 mile (320 km) radius, plus 100 miles (160 km) per level of experience.', 'Instant knowledge. Conditions should not change for at least 1D4 hours and more likely twelve.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Reveals surface weather already present or developing within the radius - fog, storms, hurricanes, ley line storms - and roughly when it will arrive, or confirms that conditions are calm.'),
  ('Dolphin: Sonic Blast', 5, 15, NULL, 'THE CATALOG ALREADY HOLDS a bare "Sonic Blast" at level 7 for 25 P.P.E., Rifts Book of Magic p.119. This is the dolphin spell, level 5 for 15, and it is stored under the Dolphin: prefix so the two do not collide - see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F26. Neither row is wrong.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.71', 'rifts', '100 feet (30.5 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant', '1D6 M.D. per level of the spell caster. One third of that figure is also inflicted as S.D.C. on the pilot of light or small armor, a bot or a vehicle - 22 M.D. does 7 S.D.C. to the pilot, 40 M.D. does 13. A large or heavily armored target passes nothing through.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'A narrow, torpedo-like sonic strike with no blast radius. It does mega-damage to the structure and bleeds a fraction through to a pilot inside lighter armor or a lighter vehicle.'),
  ('Dolphin: Sonic Stun', 6, 20, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.71', 'rifts', '50 feet (15.2 m) per level of experience.', 'Instant', '3D6 S.D.C. underwater, or 1D6 on dry land or in air, on a failed save, plus a 1-65% chance of being knocked out for 1D4 melee rounds.', 'Save versus non-lethal poison or attack, 16 or higher. A success means no damage, only ringing ears, -3 on initiative and -2 to strike, parry and dodge for 1D4 melee rounds.', NULL, NULL, 'An ultrasonic blast meant to incapacitate rather than kill. It is an S.D.C. attack and cannot hurt mega-damage armor, vehicles or structures directly, though a fraction still reaches the occupants, and it cannot penetrate a structure or vessel over fifty feet.'),
  ('Dolphin: Speed Doubler', 4, 8, NULL, NULL, 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.71', 'rifts', 'Self or one other; can be cast on a person up to 100 feet (30.5 m) away.', 'Five minutes per level of the spell caster.', NULL, 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Doubles swimming speed with no fatigue penalty. It does nothing for running on land or for flying.'),
  ('Shape Koral', 4, 10, NULL, 'The book states this spell''s level in its HEADING - Shape Koral (Level Four) - rather than on a Level: line, which the stat block does not carry at all. Its Saving Throw: field reads Special while the description two lines later says outright that there is no saving throw; the field is stored and the contradiction is recorded here.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.151', 'rifts', '30 feet (9.1 m) per level of the spell caster.', 'Permanent, or until changed again.', NULL, 'Special', NULL, NULL, 'Reshapes up to 20 lbs of Korallyte per level of the caster, each 20 lbs having 40+2D6 M.D.C., into almost any solid object - blades, armor pieces, tools, vehicle body components, containers. The caster needs a clear mental picture of the shape. The G.M. may call for a shaping roll at a base of 20% +5% per level, +10% if the caster is a koral shaper; a failed roll still produces the shape, with a cosmetic flaw rather than a failure.'),
  ('Koral Blast', 6, 20, NULL, 'The book states this spell''s level in its HEADING - Koral Blast (Level Six) - rather than on a Level: line, which the stat block does not carry at all. Its Range: field reads Touch, which is the reach needed to start it; the description gives the beam itself a range of 500 feet (152 m). Both are recorded because the field alone understates the spell.', 'import', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.152', 'rifts', 'Touch to cast; the beam itself reaches 500 feet (152 m).', 'Instant', '2D6 M.D. per ounce of Korallyte converted - two ounces 4D6, three ounces 6D6 - up to 3D6x10+12 M.D., a stated 192 points, for a full pound.', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'Works like the koral shaper''s own energy-release ability. The caster must be touching at least a pound of Korallyte and converts a chosen portion of it into a directed beam, striking at +3 while the target is -3 to dodge. Casting costs two melee actions and each blast fired afterwards is a separate action. Converting five ounces or less does not destroy the Korallyte, which regrows an ounce every 1D6 minutes; six ounces or more destroys that material permanently.')
ON CONFLICT (name) DO UPDATE SET
  level = excluded.level,
  ppe = excluded.ppe,
  ppe_note = excluded.ppe_note,
  variant_note = excluded.variant_note,
  source = excluded.source,
  source_book = excluded.source_book,
  system = excluded.system,
  range = excluded.range,
  duration = excluded.duration,
  damage = excluded.damage,
  saving_throw = excluded.saving_throw,
  area_of_effect = excluded.area_of_effect,
  casting_time = excluded.casting_time,
  description = excluded.description;

-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. Counts per
-- tradition, then the two collisions that matter most, then the total. One
-- statement each: D1 rejects a compound SELECT past five terms and rolls the
-- whole file back.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS ocean_spells FROM spells WHERE name LIKE 'Ocean: %';
SELECT COUNT(*) AS spellsongs FROM spells WHERE name LIKE 'Spellsong: %';
SELECT COUNT(*) AS dolphin_spells FROM spells WHERE name LIKE 'Dolphin: %';
SELECT name, level, ppe FROM spells WHERE name IN ('Shape Koral', 'Koral Blast') ORDER BY name;
SELECT name, level, ppe FROM spells
  WHERE name IN ('Ocean: Whirlpool', 'Water: Whirlpool', 'Dolphin: Sonic Blast', 'Sonic Blast')
  ORDER BY name;
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_spells FROM spells;

-- Records this run. One row per run rather than per file: the statement above
-- is an upsert, so this script is safe to re-run.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-underseas-spells.sql');
